# Profile: optimal_slip100 -- `optimal`, with the FOK price tolerance tightened
# from 300 bps (the config default) to 100 bps.
#
# This is the answer to "can we use limit orders": the venue takes FOK market
# orders only (IOC/GTC return -1102, measured earlier), so a resting limit is
# not available -- but every FOK carries `slippageBps`, and the order fills only
# within that band of the reference price. Tightening it is the closest thing to
# a limit: fill near the quoted price or fail and re-quote.
#
# Why 100: 53 live fills had a median of +175 bps over the DECISION quote
# (p75 +275). Note that is not the same reference the venue bounds against (the
# order-time quote), so the band observed here can exceed the configured one.
# See FINDINGS.md, "Entry slip: the limit-order experiment" for the proxy read
# and for why 100 bps is a starting point rather than a measured optimum.
#
# Revert: make config PROFILE=optimal   (nothing else differs)
# Profile: optimal_slip100 -- the EXPERIMENT arm of the slippage A/B.
#
# Identical to `optimal` except `slippage_bps=100`.
#
# Why this is the lever: the venue accepts only FOK, and rejects LIMIT quotes
# outright (-3026 "Your input param is invalid", probed 2026-09-11 17:50Z), so
# there is no resting order to place. A FOK with slippageBps IS the limit
# price -- fill now at no worse than X bps off the quote, or not at all -- and
# the venue's default is 300bps of room. At 300, the recorded 53 fills paid a
# median +175bps over the quote (p75 +275, max +487) and worse on 78%.
#
# Control arm: `optimal` (300bps), which is the record the numbers above come
# from. Compare arms on FILL RATE per round and on `ev_at_fill` (the
# `gate->fill` field in the OPEN log), not on P&L -- P&L needs hundreds of
# fills to say anything, and 'refused' is not 'lost': a refused FOK retries
# with a fresh quote and may still fill, possibly better.
#
# Knobs only -- no keys, no endpoints, nothing secret. Apply with:
#   make config PROFILE=optimal_slip100
order_type=market
slippage_bps=100
sizing_mode=fraction
stake_fraction=0.02
stake_cap_usdt=25.0
stake_floor_to_minimum=true
stake_tilt=inv_z
tilt_reference_z=0.30
tilt_min=0.5
tilt_max=2.0
min_stake_usdt=5.0
max_stake_usdt=10.0
sizing_metric=ev
stake_ev_lo=0.15
stake_ev_hi=0.45
stake_usdt=7.0
min_order_usdt=1.0
bankroll_usdt=40.0
daily_loss_cap_pct=0.0
daily_loss_cap_usdt=0.0
max_consecutive_losses=0
pricing_model=calibrated_down
up_model=calibrated
min_edge=0.01
min_quote=0.50
edge_haircut=1.0
side_filter=both
signal_persistence=2
max_tau_s=210.0
trade_on_candle_open=false
up_regime_gate=0.005
slippage_bps=100
